From df2c0f09ff7368933c54d57ce42a8daa1984a5c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:12:11 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] plugin_api: let a worker open a native field editor over
 its desktop

A Host API 2 worker whose desktop app focuses a text field had no way to
get AERA's native editor for it: the editor opens only when the user
taps the field's card on the setup page, and the desktop covers that
page.

Add kFeatureDesktopTextInput (bit 13):

- EDIT_TEXT_INPUT (worker kind 30) names an existing field of the
  committed page in request_id and opens the same editor a tap on its
  card opens, also while the desktop is open. Over the desktop, desktop
  input is suspended exactly as for Files until the editor closes by
  Done, Cancel, Back, a new page, leaving the view, the worker stopping
  or the editor being destroyed. A field that cannot be edited now is
  answered with TEXT_INPUT_RESULT kInputError.
- DISMISS_TEXT_INPUT (worker kind 31) cancels that field's editor.
  Dismissing a field that is not being edited is ignored, so every
  opened editor still ends with exactly one TEXT_INPUT_RESULT.

Both reuse TEXT_INPUT_RESULT (74) and its limits; no drafts are sent.
The kinds are valid only after the bit was acknowledged. Workers that do
not request it keep the previous behaviour, values and ACK flags.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
