diff --git a/aeraui/features/plugin_api/README.md b/aeraui/features/plugin_api/README.md
index 3231a3fb..7d4791f3 100644
--- a/aeraui/features/plugin_api/README.md
+++ b/aeraui/features/plugin_api/README.md
@@ -337,3 +337,30 @@ page or a detached view cancels an open editor; stopping/crashing the runtime
 closes it. Background workers cannot open the keyboard or read the draft.
 Field values are retained with a live background runtime, but persistence
 across process restarts remains the plugin's responsibility.
+
+### Native editing over the desktop (optional)
+
+Request `kFeatureDesktopTextInput` (bit 13) with `kFeatureTextInput` and check
+the ACK. It lets the worker open the native editor of one of its text input
+fields itself, also while the desktop covers the setup page, for example when
+its desktop app focuses a field. It is the native modal path: incremental
+typing into a desktop app uses the desktop keyboard and `PLAY_KEY` instead.
+The kinds below are valid only after the bit was acknowledged; an
+unacknowledged one closes the session. Without the bit nothing changes.
+
+- `EDIT_TEXT_INPUT` (worker kind 30): `request_id` is the field ID of an input
+  on the committed page; value and flags are zero and both strings empty. AERA
+  opens the same editor as tapping the card, with the field's title, value,
+  mode and limit. Over an open desktop, desktop input is suspended as for
+  Files (see Desktop integration) until the editor closes by any path. If the
+  field is unknown or disabled, the view is not in the foreground, a page is
+  being assembled, or another modal or operation is open, the reply is
+  `TEXT_INPUT_RESULT` with kInputError. A request for the field already being
+  edited changes nothing.
+- `DISMISS_TEXT_INPUT` (worker kind 31): the same field ID and zero/empty
+  fields close that editor as Cancel does. Dismissing a field that is not
+  being edited is ignored.
+
+Each opened editor ends with exactly one `TEXT_INPUT_RESULT`: kInputSubmitted
+with the confirmed text, or kInputCancelled. The 255-code-point limit and the
+absence of drafts are unchanged.
diff --git a/aeraui/features/plugin_api/protocol.hpp b/aeraui/features/plugin_api/protocol.hpp
